    {
      "id": 250364,
      "name": "dprcooke",
      "username": "dprcooke",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dprcooke/{size}/1961_2.png",
      "created_at": "2023-01-18T15:59:39.664Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Glad I’m not the only GM who has trouble coming up with environment-related things, on the fly or otherwise.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Environment is the part I have the most trouble coming with.  At least ahead of time while building the issue.  Everything else is very story-related (the villain has a story, the adventure has a story), but the Environment doesn’t.  At least in the planning stage / for me.  <em>During play</em>, working off my players and what they’re doing, I can usually come up with some good stuff.  But while building the adventure?  Not so much.</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2023-01-18T16:01:52.849Z",
